    "tool_subscribe_states": {
      "_comment": "call.subscribe(event, args) from a tool that declares the event, per access and caller: the Subscription's state (and reason), whether the block carries a native line telling the client what to subscribe to, and whether the SDK asks Wakeshift (POST /event-subscriptions). access: tools (crawl.finished-like, no setting), personal, public, authorize_allows / authorize_refuses (deploy.finished, allowing only u1). caller: bridged (Claude Code: recognized as a conversation the SDK subscribes) or native (an MCP Events client that subscribes itself). Arguments: crawl.finished {job: j1}, deploy.finished {env: prod}, a personal event {table: oak}, a public event {channel: eng}. error: call.subscribe throws UsageError with that code. logs: the warnings.json code logged (once per tool and reason). created has id, user, session (redacted when printed) and recognized; native has user and recognized; unavailable has reason; disabled has nothing. On a disabled client every row is state disabled with nothing asked (disabled-client.json).",
